{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"papers\": [\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:19758982\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 31,\n      \"center\": \"Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre, Wilfrid Laurier University, Waterloo, Ontario, Canada\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:24727559\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 27,\n      \"center\": \"Sun Life Financial Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre, Wilfrid Laurier University, Waterloo, Ontario, Canada\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:25730121\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 47,\n      \"center\": \"Sun Life Financial Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre, Wilfrid Laurier University, Waterloo, Ontario, Canada\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:21997389\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 10,\n      \"center\": \"National Hospital for Neurology and Neurosurgery / UCL Institute of Neurology, London, UK\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:28505983\",\n      \"kind\": \"review_meta\",\n      \"n_patients\": null,\n      \"center\": \"\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:30800094\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 24,\n      \"center\": \"National Hospital for Neurology and Neurosurgery, London, UK\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:33101404\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 55,\n      \"center\": \"Guangzhou First People's Hospital, Guangzhou, China\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:34744665\",\n      \"kind\": \"review_meta\",\n      \"n_patients\": 538,\n      \"center\": \"\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:37239209\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 23,\n      \"center\": \"Union Hospital of Fujian Medical University, Fuzhou, China\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"2019-02至2022-07\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"DOI:10.1101/2025.04.22.650006\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 2,\n      \"center\": \"University Hospital Würzburg, Würzburg, Germany\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pid\": \"PMID:41654501\",\n      \"kind\": \"primary_patient\",\n      \"n_patients\": 2,\n      \"center\": \"University Hospital Würzburg, Würzburg, Germany\",\n      \"recruitment\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"relations\": [\n    {\n      \"a\": \"PMID:19758982\",\n      \"b\": \"PMID:24727559\",\n      \"relation\": \"unknown\",\n      \"basis\": \"两篇论文均来自Wilfrid Laurier University的Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre，研究对象均包括PD-FOG、PD-nonFOG和健康对照。2010年研究分组为15、16、16人，2014年为14、13、14人，分组规模非常接近，存在使用同一患者数据库或部分重复招募的可能。但2014年摘要总人数42与分组人数之和41不一致，且未找到明确的患者身份对应或既有队列复用声明，不能认定为same_cohort或partial_overlap。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"a\": \"PMID:19758982\",\n      \"b\": \"PMID:25730121\",\n      \"relation\": \"unknown\",\n      \"basis\": \"两篇论文均来自Wilfrid Laurier University的Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre，均由Almeida参与。2010年研究包含31名PD患者，2015年研究包含47名PD患者。2015年论文使用Almeida与Lebold（2010）所述的FOG临床确认方法，提示研究团队及患者来源可能存在联系，但引用既有评估方法不等于复用患者。没有明确的队列重叠声明或患者身份信息。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"a\": \"PMID:24727559\",\n      \"b\": \"PMID:25730121\",\n      \"relation\": \"unknown\",\n      \"basis\": \"两篇论文均在Waterloo的同一Movement Disorders Research and Rehabilitation Centre开展，共享Pieruccini-Faria、Jones和Almeida三位作者，发表时间相近。2014年分析27名PD患者，2015年分析47名PD患者，均区分FOG与non-FOG亚组。可能存在同一患者数据库的重复使用或扩展招募，但没有直接证据确认患者重叠。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"a\": \"PMID:21997389\",\n      \"b\": \"PMID:30800094\",\n      \"relation\": \"unknown\",\n      \"basis\": \"两篇研究均来自伦敦National Hospital for Neurology and Neurosurgery及UCL研究团队，共享Limousin、Peters和Day等研究人员。2012年研究包括10名接受STN-DBS的FOG患者，2019年研究包括24名接受长期STN-DBS（超过4年）的患者。两篇研究均采用门框行走任务和三维步态运动学分析，且研究中心及患者来源相同，存在部分患者重叠的合理可能。但没有患者身份对应、明确的既有队列复用声明或足以确认重叠的招募时间资料。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"a\": \"DOI:10.1101/2025.04.22.650006\",\n      \"b\": \"PMID:41654501\",\n      \"relation\": \"same_work\",\n      \"basis\": \"2025年bioRxiv预印本与2026年NPJ Parkinson's Disease正式论文为同一学术成果的不同版本。标题高度一致，核心摘要、研究问题、6-OHDA帕金森病大鼠模型、神经行为特征分析方法以及两名接受双侧STN-DBS的PD患者验证数据一致。正式版于2026年2月7日发表。作者名单存在版本调整，但不构成独立研究的依据。两篇论文中的两名患者应视为同一批患者，不能重复计数。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "236368e1-b24f-4077-ad4b-6d440d2ad33c", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261114T100429758647Z", "elapsed_seconds": 526.094, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T10:13:15.867696+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "244f258188385f26af570ae79fcd7701312e4a0cf5d524c75c1639c064dff591", "attachment_count": 0}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 0, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc